From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:05:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Screensaver mode: an overlay at the window's resolution

A retained scene of rectangles, text and images that the plugin describes
(screensaver.overlay: set, remove, clear, fade, measureText, setDefaultFonts, scale), in game
pixels. It is rasterized on the CPU at the output size into a premultiplied buffer, only
where it changed, with text from FreeType (the TTF port), and composited with real alpha
just before present: an SDL texture in the software engine, a textured quad in OpenGL.
Fades run in the engine. The overlay shows only in the mode and is cleared on leaving.
